      "data": {
        "text": "**Developing Python Files**\n\nI'm currently focused on developing the Python files for the managed model platform workflow. Right now, I am going to develop `invoke_platform_model.py` and then I will develop the rest of the 10 files. I'm making sure that the \"scored\" files, SAME-SCENARIO and LATER-STEP, are using an external provider. I'm also ensuring that AWS is used.\n\n\n**Defining Python Files**\n\nI've defined the ten Python files and their roles in the workflow. I'm starting implementation with `invoke_platform_model.py`, utilizing AWS Bedrock via `boto3`. I've outlined the concrete providers for the \"scored\" files: Google Cloud Natural Language API for safety, Google Cloud Translation API for localization, and Google Cloud Vertex AI Embeddings. Helper files for model interaction and data models are also planned.\n\n\n**Outlining File Structure**\n\nI'm now outlining the structure of all ten Python files. I've chosen `invoke_platform_model.py` as the starting point, leveraging `boto3` for AWS Bedrock integration. I've also assigned concrete external providers to each \"scored\" file, including Google Cloud Natural Language API, Google Cloud Translation API, and Google Cloud Vertex AI Embeddings. Helper files are planned for model interaction and data models. My focus is now on implementing these files sequentially. I'll be sure to use the helper files throughout.\n\n\n",
